<title>GERMANY: SKI JUMPING-WORLD CUP HIGH HILL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SKI JUMPING-WORLD CUP HIGH HILL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>WILLINGEN, Germany 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in a World Cup high hill ski jumping event on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Hiroya Saitoh (Japan)	 122.0 points (122.5 metres)</p>
<p> 2. Dieter Thoma (Germany)	   116.5 (122.5)</p>
<p> 3. Roar Ljoekelsoy (Norway)	 112.1 (117.0)</p>
<p> 4. Frank Reichel (Germany)	  110.8 (118.5)</p>
<p> 5. Primoz Peterka (Slowenia)	110.7 (116.5)</p>
<p> 6. Kristian Brenden (Norway)	109.7 (116.5)</p>
<p> 7. Kazuyoshi Funaki (Japan)	 107.2 (114.0)</p>
<p> 8. Lasse Ottesen (Norway)	   105.8 (116.0)</p>
<p> 9. Hein-Arne Mathiesen (Norway)   102.0 (112.5)</p>
<p>10. Roman Krenek (Czech republic) 101.7 (114.0)</p>
<p>Note: The event was limited to one jump because of poor weather conditions and darkness.</p>
</text>
